// Probe 09 — Cluster III canonical: `??` result inside a format string
//
// The shape:
//     msg = "got: {h.items[0] ?? \"x\"}";
//
// Format strings build into a function-scope `__work_N: text` buffer.
// The `??` inside the interpolation creates its own `_ncc_M` block.  The
// OpFormatText op reads from the block's result Str into the work buffer.
//
// Two interaction possibilities:
//   1. The format-string lowering materialises into __work_N BEFORE the
//      block's OpFreeText fires → the work buffer captures the right
//      bytes, dangling Str on stack is harmless after copy.  Cluster I
//      fix is sufficient.
//   2. The format-string lowering reads the block's Str AFTER the block's
//      OpFreeText (same dangling-pointer escape) → cluster III is a
//      distinct mechanism in the format-string machinery.
//
// Expected (rustc 1.96 / macOS): unknown; if FAIL, mechanism (2);
// if PASS, mechanism (1).  Both outcomes are diagnostic.
// Pairing: diff against 02 — same `??` inside, different consumer.
// Status: cluster III canonical probe.

struct H { items: vector<text> }

fn main() {
  h = H { items: [] };
  h.items += ["present"];
  msg = "got: {h.items[0] ?? \"x\"}";
  assert(msg == "got: present", "probe 09: got '{msg}', want 'got: present'");
  println("probe 09 PASSED");
}
